WEBVTT

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.460
Well then... Here goes.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:24.580
You did it!

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:27.250
That was some perfect control
over your magical power.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.040
So, what are we going to do with the ice
now that you've pulverized it?

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.880
Well, you see...

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.460
How pretty...!

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:40.630
What is it?

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:42.250
It's called shaved ice.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:43.250
Give it a try.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.130
So nice and cold!

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.580
It's sweet!

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:50.830
I can feel it all throughout
my exhausted body!

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:53.130
How delicious!

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:56.580
Shaved ice is really good
when you eat it down all at once.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:57.630
Is that so?

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:59.330
But that feels like such a waste.

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:01.080
I made extra, so no worries.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.750
Then let's go for it...!

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:07.670
My head, it hurts!

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:08.880
What's going on?!

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.750
Yes, that's right.

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:14.130
Just why does it hurt like that?

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.710
Ms. Sarasa...

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.250
I thought it would be good to have
you experience it at least once.

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:21.420
Ms. Owner...

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:24.750
Hey there.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.920
Ah, welcome.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.290
I'd like to have you buy
some ingredients again.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:30.170
Of course!

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:31.420
And I need some potions.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:33.630
On it! Thank you!

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:35.460
Could I have a moment?

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:47.830
Kyou kara mieru yo chiisai hoshi

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:51.250
Terashitete ne mune no naka o

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:54.540
Naite waratte kagaiyaite

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.750
Udemakutte arukidasou

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:59.960
(Kitto alright nayamu wa go sign)

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.210
(Kichin to yarimashou)

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:09.580
Jiyuu sugiru tte nante fujiyuu nan deshou

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:12.920
Datte tokenai no yo

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:16.330
Rironchi jikkenchi spiral

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:18.420
Maido utedo katte mo

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.000
(Nani o tameshite mite mo)

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.670
Nengan kanatte shikuhakku

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:23.500
(Cheat ja nai yo life hack)

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:27.000
Harete ippo fumidaseru license

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.250
Kore kara ga hajimari

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:33.500
Kyou kara mieru yo chiisai hoshi

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.880
Terashitete ne mune no naka o

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:40.250
Naite waratte kagaiyaite

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:42.830
Shigoto no mae wa shinkokyuu

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:47.000
Hibike te o nobashita shintenchi

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.330
Yume wa kitto te no naka

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:53.750
Kitto dekiru original

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:56.460
Door o akete welcome de ikou

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.960
(Sore ja koko ga start)

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:02.460
(Kitto alright nayamu wa go sign)

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:04.880
(Kichin to yarimashou)

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:09.960
What is it you wanted to discuss?

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:14.420
Well, it's about the merchant
who's come here to this village.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:15.580
A merchant?

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:19.250
Yeah, he borrowed a house
in the area recently...

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:20.420
That's the one!

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:24.670
You see, that merchant's been
gathering up frostfang bat fangs.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:27.540
He's been buying them for
ten percent more than you do.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:28.420
Huh?

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:31.500
It's true that we haven't had many people
coming to sell them lately...

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.920
And our stock may well be
decreasing, sure enough.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:35.790
To be honest, aside from those of us
who've been with you the whole time,

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:37.170
everyone's selling to him.

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:39.130
Can this stand, Ms. Owner?

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:41.250
Well, it's only natural
that everyone would go there

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:42.670
if they can sell their goods for more.

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:44.170
You're taking this too lightly...!

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.790
Still, normally you would have
the proper manners

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:49.210
to at least discuss the matter with us first.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:52.750
And I certainly don't want to see the plan

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.210
we finally got running with
the cooling hats ruined.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:57.540
I've actually got one more
thing to mention...

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:02.000
It's about when I went to go take a look...

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:11.710
There was a group
talking there all friendly.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:14.080
Their faces were hidden, but...

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:15.830
Those were bandits.

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:18.420
Bandits?!

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:20.250
There are bandits here in the village?!

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:24.130
No, I went and followed them after that,
but they kept on going and left.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.290
That certainly is a concern...

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:30.380
So is that merchant
a part of the bandit crew?

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:34.380
If he was, he wouldn't use
such a roundabout method.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:36.670
This is a proper sales tactic.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.250
Is that so...?

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:42.210
But you were buying them for a bit of
a high price to begin with, weren't you?

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:45.250
So can you really turn a profit
going even higher still?

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:47.880
It would be difficult.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:50.380
If you traveled to the capital
it would be one thing,

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:53.710
but when you account for the transport costs
it would definitely put you in the red.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:55.080
Then why...?

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:57.040
I'm not sure what his objective is.

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:03.880
What if that merchant needs to gather fangs
by whatever means possible?

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:07.540
Like if he took a contract in advance
to prepare a certain amount.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:07.210
<b>Merchant: I'll absolutely get you 100 fangs.</b>

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.960
But then he wasn't able to do so.

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:08.750
<b>Gatherer: I didn't get any at all...</b>

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:09.960
<b>Oh no...!</b>

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:13.210
So buying for a high price
would be cheaper than

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:15.330
the penalty for breach of contract?

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:17.880
Yeah. Or he could be
manipulating the market price.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:21.630
He could have predicted the price would
go up for summer and bought a lot up,

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:22.290
<b>Merchant: One will be 1,500 rhea.</b>

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:24.000
but thanks to the supplies from this village,

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:24.000
<b>Alchemist: You can buy them for</b>

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:24.000
<b>1,000 rhea in Yok Village.</b>

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.080
that didn't happen.

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:28.830
So he could be buying them himself
to cut off the supply?

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:29.920
Right.

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:33.960
But the fangs themselves shouldn't sell
for much on the market...

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:37.790
We've been storing all the ones
we haven't used in the cooling hats.

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:42.630
At any rate, neither of those explanations
cover why there are bandits around.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:45.330
In that case...

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:47.210
What about a grudge?

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:50.670
Huh?! I don't remember
earning any grudges!

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:54.080
That's right! Nobody could
possibly hate Ms. Sarasa!

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:57.330
Lorea, it's certainly unreasonable,
but you can end up with

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:59.670
somebody hating you even if you
don't do anything to cause it.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:03.460
Like if we take someone else out there
making a profit on those fangs...

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:07.080
What if your father ended up
being hated as such?

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:09.000
My dad?!

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.250
Ah, that was just an example...

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:16.250
It's true, he's increasing
the stock of items he handles

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:19.130
thanks to the sales from the cooling hats...

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:23.250
So you're saying he could be
attacked by bandits because of that?!

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:24.540
Come on, Lorea...

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:26.670
We were just talking hypothetically.

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:27.710
I'm sorry...

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:33.960
The truth is, my grandpa and grandma
were both killed by bandits...

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:41.040
So if something were to happen
to my dad too...

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.670
My apologies.
I chose my example poorly.

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:46.460
It'll be alright.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:49.830
Mr. Darna doesn't really
stand out badly or anything,

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:52.540
so I can't imagine anyone
hating him that much!

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:54.290
You really mean it?!

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:56.130
Yeah! However...

00:06:56.710 --> 00:07:00.920
Why don't we have him stop heading to town
for now, just to be on the safe side?

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.250
I'll let him know.

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:03.960
Don't worry.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:06.080
Even if bandits do show up...

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:14.830
I'll be sure to punish them.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:16.330
Really?!

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.460
Yeah!

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:21.420
So, regardless of his motive, how do you
intend to handle that merchant?

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:22.960
Well...

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:26.500
Why don't I try raising
my buy prices as well to start?

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:28.960
Sure enough, if you buy for the same cost

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:31.750
you will definitely get the sales,
as you've earned greater trust.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:35.210
But then won't you suffer
loses as a result?

00:07:35.210 --> 00:07:38.000
We'll still be alright at
the current sale price.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:41.290
As long as I don't have any
screwups in my alchemy, that is.

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:43.040
What if something does fail?

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:45.790
Dozens of sales worth of profit
will be lost all at once.

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:47.170
Huh?!

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:49.790
That's why artifacts are so expensive.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:53.170
Normally, prices are set with
one out of every two attempts

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:54.750
ending in failure in mind.

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:56.170
I had no idea.

00:07:56.170 --> 00:08:00.130
Still, I won't screw up when it comes to
something like a cooling hat.

00:08:00.130 --> 00:08:03.170
After all, I'm Ophelia Millis's apprentice!

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:05.710
Huh?!

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:07.210
Eh...?

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:09.630
Th-th-that master class alchemist?!

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:11.210
Did I not mention that?

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:12.210
I never heard it!

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:16.040
Then that woman back then
was Ophelia Millis?

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:18.080
Is she famous?

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:21.630
Master class is the highest rank
for all alchemists!

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:25.080
And even among them,
Lady Ophelia is someone special!

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.750
Ophelia Millis is so famed

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:30.380
that her name is well known
even outside of alchemist circles.

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:31.460
Right?

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:32.710
Yes, right!

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:36.000
Ophelia Millis is amazing!

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:38.460
Come on, calm yourself!

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:42.540
I got a bit worked up.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:44.210
Let's get back on topic.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:47.630
So the plan is to raise your purchase rates
to the same as that merchant?

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:48.750
That's right.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.130
Hopefully that will get him to give up.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:54.130
But if he continues to resist
and raises his rates further,

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:58.500
I'll keep on hunting frostfang bats myself
and increase the supply.

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:00.880
Then you can sell them all off to him!

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:02.130
That's a great idea.

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:04.670
If I ask for help from Mr. Andre's group,

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:07.130
we should be able to gather
several hundred fangs each day.

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:12.080
So unless he has quite the fortune,
that should cause his finances to run out.

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:16.580
It will be a race to see if the
frostfang bats in the caves run out first,

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:19.670
or his funds do...

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:22.670
Scary!

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:24.380
I'm just joking.

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:26.290
Really...?

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.500
Sarasa!

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:40.790
Your mother and father, they were
attacked by bandits at the pass!

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:49.250
That will be 13,000 rhea!

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:50.750
I'll be back again.

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:52.000
We'll be waiting!

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:54.080
We've been able to buy more fangs again.

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:56.540
Yes, the raise in prices is working perfectly!

00:09:56.750 --> 00:09:58.210
Ms. Owner!

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:00.290
They raised their prices too!

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:05.330
Oh my, it seems they lack the
foresight needed to plan ahead.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:09.080
Ooh, just like a real mastermind!

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.540
So how much did they raise them?

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:12.830
By fifty percent.

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:15.790
And when we went there
to sell the fangs...

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:17.630
Thanks for your business.

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:20.540
You certainly bought them for quite a bit.

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:23.790
That's because I have
business rivals all around.

00:10:24.210 --> 00:10:28.380
Still, they seem to be having
quite a tough time...

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:30.960
A tough time?

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:32.500
What did he mean?

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:35.130
He seems to think that
you've been having trouble

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:37.710
and raised the prices because
you can't get ahold of any fangs.

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:41.460
In other words... I'm his target?

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:43.290
That may be so.

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:47.790
How amusing...

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:49.330
Ms. Sarasa...?

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:51.750
It's nothing to worry about.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:55.460
Well then, we'll start the plan
tomorrow everyone.

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:57.670
I'll be counting on your assistance!

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:14.580
Well then, let's be off!

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:18.580
Wait, what's with the outfit, Sarasa?!

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:21.170
Oh, for today I'm not Sarasa.

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:23.960
I'm the rookie gatherer Novicessa!

00:11:23.210 --> 00:11:25.080
<b>Novicessa</b>

00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:25.080
But why?!

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:28.130
Because I can't let my opponent
know what I'm up to!

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:29.380
So I don't want to stand out!

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:31.880
Who's ever heard of
such a suspicious rookie?!

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:36.500
Here they come!

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:47.170
You all did great.

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:50.500
Nah, you hunted down
more than anyone, Sarasa.

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:53.710
That's just because I used my
magical power for physical enhancement.

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:55.750
Also, it's Novicessa.

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:57.920
What, so we're even keeping that up here?

00:11:57.920 --> 00:11:59.960
There isn't anyone around.

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:03.460
Are you perhaps enjoying
yourself, Ms. Novicessa?

00:12:03.460 --> 00:12:08.380
Of course not. I'm just trying to
deal with a greedy merchant is all.

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:12.330
"Run an honest business,"
is my family motto, after all.

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:13.750
Motto?

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:16.420
Ms. Novicessa, your family
were merchants?

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:17.330
Yes.

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:21.170
My parents were killed by bandits, though.

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:24.420
Please don't tell Lorea.

00:12:25.710 --> 00:12:29.540
It was definitely sad losing my parents,

00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:32.710
but it's not like I've faced
misfortune ever since.

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:36.080
Since I'm running a shop,
I want to run it honestly,

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:38.580
just like my father tried to do.

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:42.630
And so I have to deal with any obstacles
that get in the way of that!

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:47.830
Then we'll have to keep on lending you
our aid to help see it through.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:50.290
I'll be counting on you!

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.630
According to another gatherer,
that merchant was shouting,

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:59.580
"Just how long is she going to
keep holding out?!"

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:03.130
And apparently he's headed out by carriage
numerous times in the past few days.

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:06.830
He must be heading out of the village
to deal with the fangs.

00:13:06.830 --> 00:13:11.130
So his finances are starting to run out,
just like you planned, right?

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:14.830
Still, if he's able to procure
more money from outside,

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:16.630
this fight could turn dirty.

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:23.580
Ms. Iris, where would you sell
the fangs obtained in this village?

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:27.920
Huh? Well... the closest place
would be South Straug.

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:29.330
Right?

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:32.330
And as for the alchemist located there...

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:34.750
She's your acquaintance, right?

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:37.630
Yes! I'll send a letter
to ask for her assistance!

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:41.130
You're always so thoroughly prepared!

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:42.830
Even though you're so tiny.

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:45.460
You didn't need that last part!

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:48.000
I'm going to keep on growing!

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:56.540
Why don't I take these
in order to pay off your debt?!

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:58.380
Don't say such frightening things!

00:13:58.380 --> 00:14:03.250
Even alchemists can't just take away
and add things like that, right?!

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:05.880
We'll just see about that...

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:09.830
H-hold on...!

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.250
I'm just joking.

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:16.330
If I felt like it, I could always use potions
to do something about my figure.

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:17.920
R-really?

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:20.540
That's an alchemist for you.
Impressive as always.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:23.210
So Ms. Owner, why haven't you...?

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:29.830
Ah, I have no intention of unnaturally
changing this body my parents left me.

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:34.830
That's why I'm still hoping
for natural growth.

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:38.960
You truly respect your parents,
don't you, Ms. Owner?

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:41.960
Well, I lost them when I was still a child,

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:44.580
and they were often away from home,

00:14:44.580 --> 00:14:47.130
so I don't have that many memories...

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:50.330
But I'm certain they were parents
worthy of my respect.

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:53.750
Even after becoming an orphan,
you kept on striving as hard as you could.

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:56.330
I have great respect for you, Ms. Owner.

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:58.630
Wh-what are you saying,
all of a sudden...?!

00:14:58.630 --> 00:15:00.540
O-of course I put in a lot of effort,

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:04.290
but all sorts of people
helped me out too, so, well...

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:09.170
It feels embarassing,
getting praised like that!

00:15:13.210 --> 00:15:15.500
At any rate, we just need to
keep going a little more!

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:18.750
I'll head out to South Straug tomorrow.

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.500
Here you are.

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:28.040
Thank you, Ms. Filiorne.

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:32.830
Fi, could I ask you to
prepare lunch for Sarasa too?

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:34.420
Ah, don't worry about me...!

00:15:34.420 --> 00:15:39.580
It's fine. If I'm not careful,
Nora will skip lunch all the time.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:42.790
Now then, we were discussing
that merchant.

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:45.380
Right... Has he come here?

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:46.420
Yes...

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:50.790
Though the market price had fallen
and gotten rather low, he still sold them.

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:53.250
He seemed rather cornered.

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:54.710
So it seems.

00:15:54.710 --> 00:15:58.420
I was curious too, and so I went ahead
and looked into him.

00:15:58.420 --> 00:16:00.380
Did you find anything out.

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:02.880
Yes, all sorts of things.

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:07.420
To start with, his name is Gree Dilly.

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:11.170
He runs a shop here in town
called the Dilly Company.

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:17.290
They primarily deal in alchemic ingredients
and artifacts, as well as potions.

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:19.540
Potions too?

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:21.170
It's curious, isn't it?

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:24.500
Someone who isn't an alchemist
handling potions would involve a high risk

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:29.420
in terms of effectiveness,
preservation, and overall quality.

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:31.580
That's very much true. However...

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:34.290
Has he employed an alchemist?

00:16:34.290 --> 00:16:36.380
Something similar to that...

00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:41.540
Apparently he makes alchemists
who owe him a debt work it off under him.

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:43.250
Debt?

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:46.500
He seems to have brought them all down.

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:50.380
For example, messing with their
ingredients to make them fail.

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:51.960
How awful!

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:53.750
And he still hasn't been caught?!

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:55.500
He may be a real piece of work,

00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:58.000
but he hasn't broken any laws,
at least not openly.

00:16:58.920 --> 00:17:02.630
And what makes things even more
troublesome is that Gree hires bandits.

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:04.290
Bandits?!

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:08.380
He uses them to threaten
the alchemists he entraps,

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:11.670
and even sometimes
has them attack people.

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:21.250
And he always targets
young kids like you, too.

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:25.920
Novice alchemists have less experience
and are more easily tricked.

00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:27.420
I see...

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:31.460
So his goal right from the start
was to force me into debt.

00:17:31.790 --> 00:17:34.830
He wanted to get ahold of you
and use you for all you're worth.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:38.420
But this time, he chose poorly.

00:17:38.420 --> 00:17:41.580
I'm a novice too. Just a rookie.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:43.330
A mere rookie would never make it

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:45.500
all the way here to me
in a case like this.

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:51.130
It's a real hassle having a tactless merchant
go around messing with market prices,

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:53.830
so I'd definitely like to use
the opportunity to take him down.

00:17:53.830 --> 00:17:55.170
I'll help out.

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:58.670
Right now, I'm feeling incredibly angry.

00:18:00.710 --> 00:18:02.380
Don't worry...

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:04.540
I know you can handle it!

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:06.500
Still, please take care.

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:08.290
Right!

00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:25.250
You have some real guts,
to go and attack an alchemist.

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:27.960
Ha! You've sure got a big head!

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:31.290
Even nobles are just prey
without any guards around!

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:35.630
Hand over all your cash,
and we'll at least let you live.

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:38.170
And what if I resist?

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:39.170
Oh?

00:18:39.170 --> 00:18:42.580
Are you raring to have a go, little missie?

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:45.170
Have you ever stopped to consider

00:18:45.170 --> 00:18:48.330
just how hard we alchemists work
to obtain our licenses?

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:50.250
About how we feel?

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:52.040
Huh? What're you going on about?

00:18:52.040 --> 00:18:53.500
As if we'd give a damn!

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:57.170
We just like stealing stuff
that doesn't belong to us!

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:04.080
Sarasa, I can't ever forgive bandits
because they go and steal away

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:07.830
what people work
so desperately to obtain.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:13.710
We had a real stupid rookie alchemist
who tried to stand up to us before too.

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:15.290
Remind me, what happened to them?

00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:16.540
We killed em!

00:19:18.830 --> 00:19:20.830
Among my fellow merchants,

00:19:20.830 --> 00:19:23.460
a lot of acquaintances of mine
have lost their lives to them.

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:25.670
We'll give you one more chance.

00:19:25.670 --> 00:19:28.290
Hand over everything you've got.

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:30.880
Come on, say something!

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:33.040
If you turn a blind eye towards them,

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:35.460
they'll cause someone else
misfortune down the line.

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:39.170
Make sure you remember this, Sarasa.

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:42.130
If you see a bandit, then make sure...

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:47.420
Little brat!

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:48.960
Never mind! Just kill her!

00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:50.170
Force bullet!

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:54.250
Why you...!

00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:04.710
What?!

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:06.460
H-hey!

00:20:14.210 --> 00:20:16.210
Hold on! Please, wait!

00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:20.040
L-let's make a deal!
We'll tell you who hired us!

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:21.630
It was a merchant! His name's Gree...!

00:20:21.630 --> 00:20:23.250
Never mind that.

00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:28.960
I can't imagine your testimony will be
any use in catching that merchant.

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:31.960
W-we'll give you all our cash!

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:33.540
I'm begging you, let us go!

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:34.630
But why?

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:39.170
If I defeat you, it will be mine regardless.

00:20:56.630 --> 00:20:58.250
Welcome!

00:20:58.540 --> 00:21:02.040
Listen, I'm a merchant
staying here in the village...!

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:04.040
Ah, Mr. Gree Dilly.

00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:06.000
I've heard all about you.

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:07.630
Is that so?

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:11.710
You see, I was actually thinking of
leaving this village soon.

00:21:11.710 --> 00:21:14.170
My, how sad!

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:18.420
I hear it's become so lively
around here thanks to you!

00:21:20.080 --> 00:21:22.130
S-so you see, I was wondering

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:25.580
if you could purchase
my frostfang bat fangs...

00:21:25.580 --> 00:21:27.210
My apologies,

00:21:27.210 --> 00:21:30.170
but the marketplace is so flooded now
that we don't have any need for them.

00:21:31.290 --> 00:21:33.330
Can't you do anything?!

00:21:34.630 --> 00:21:37.000
Very well. In that case,
I suppose I can buy ten of them.

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:39.380
I have nearly ten thousand of the things!

00:21:39.380 --> 00:21:41.250
My, how amazing!

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:43.710
Well then, it will take four days
to provide an appraisal.

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:45.960
That won't be soon enough!

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:48.920
How troubling...

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:54.210
Did you perhaps take out a debt
from some nasty people?

00:21:55.420 --> 00:21:58.460
If you're in that much of a hurry,
then I could buy them on the spot.

00:21:58.460 --> 00:22:01.250
The estimated value will be
quite a bit lower, though.

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:02.460
Please...!

00:22:02.710 --> 00:22:04.210
Well then, here you are.

00:22:04.750 --> 00:22:05.960
Huh?!

00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:07.460
Don't mess with me!

00:22:07.460 --> 00:22:09.920
Those fangs have spread
not only throughout the area,

00:22:09.920 --> 00:22:11.920
but the neighboring town as well.

00:22:11.920 --> 00:22:15.000
And so the market price has plummeted.

00:22:21.080 --> 00:22:22.420
Mr. Gree Dilly!

00:22:23.540 --> 00:22:25.080
Come back anytime!

00:22:25.460 --> 00:22:27.000
As if I'd ever be caught dead back here!

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:34.330
It's been about a week now, hasn't it?

00:22:34.710 --> 00:22:36.790
I wonder what became of that merchant.

00:22:36.790 --> 00:22:38.500
Hopefully he's still alive.

00:22:38.500 --> 00:22:42.500
Still, there certainly is
a lot to running a business.

00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:44.540
Too much, if you ask me...

00:22:44.540 --> 00:22:47.920
Ms. Ophelia bought
the fangs though, right?

00:22:47.920 --> 00:22:50.000
So that must have made for quite the profit.

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:51.580
I can't deny that.

00:22:51.880 --> 00:22:53.710
What are you gonna do with the money?

00:22:53.710 --> 00:22:56.960
I'll use part of it to help out
the alchemists who were victims.

00:22:56.960 --> 00:23:00.790
Ms. Leonora and I took on their debt.

00:23:00.790 --> 00:23:02.250
Is that so?

00:23:02.250 --> 00:23:03.830
You sure are kind.

00:23:03.830 --> 00:23:08.330
Oh, no, there were strings attached
when it came to helping them out.

00:23:08.630 --> 00:23:10.960
So they'll listen to plenty of
unreasonable requests.

00:23:13.880 --> 00:23:16.500
So how much is the interest?

00:23:16.960 --> 00:23:21.290
I'm sure you don't need to worry
about such things, Ms. Owner.

00:23:21.880 --> 00:23:24.420
Well, that's true...

00:23:24.420 --> 00:23:25.750
I'm glad.

00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:29.210
You really are the sort of person
I thought you were, Ms. Sarasa!

